## Critical vs. Non-Critical Classification

### Critical (would cause wrong agent decisions):
- **G5, G6, G7** (core_emergence_critic missing all_codes, core_concern, object_of_study) — critic can't evaluate if a candidate is actually "core"
- **G9, G10** (selective_reduction_critic missing core_concern, core_category) — critic can't verify reduction is around the right concern
- **G15, G16** (labeler missing own previous output in refinement loop) — cannot do targeted refinement
- **G31, G32** (literature_critic missing theory + fragments) — can't verify forcing claims
- **G36** (applicability_critic missing theory) — can't verify genuineness

### Medium (weakens evaluation quality):
- **G1-G4** (main_concern_critic missing memos, RQ, OQ)
- **G12-G14** (database critics missing RQ, relationships)
- **G17-G18** (refinement loop missing structured context)
- **G27-G29** (writing_critic missing study context)

### Low (minor, nice-to-have):
- **G19** (legacy incident extractor — largely deprecated)
- **G20-G21** (pattern verifier missing RQ, coding style)
- **G30** (gap_feeler missing RQ)
- **G34-G35** (applicability engine missing RQ, core_concern)

